 "title": "Maharashtra CM Devendra Fadnavis writes to the Union Civil Aviation Ministry (letter of Wed 11 Nov 2026) opposing Mumbai airport operator MIAL's proposal to shift about a third of CSMIA's international operations to Navi Mumbai International Airport from the summer 2027 schedule (end of March 2027): 14 international destinations incl. Doha, Jeddah, Muscat and Riyadh, to make room to rebuild Terminal 1 (15 million passengers a year; Fadnavis's letter says the current plan replaces it with a new terminal by Dec 2030). He asks that no international flight be discontinued or diverted, says both airports should run independently, and proposes building the new T1B first, moving T1A operations into it, then rebuilding T1A. IndiGo, Air India and Akasa agreed to move some services; foreign airlines object; the operator says about 91% of traffic is unaffected.",
